ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE GRAIN MANAGEMENT ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Grain Management Act and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended on June 30, 2005; January 31, 2008>

Article 2 (Cereals, etc.)
(1) “Cereals and tubers prescribed by Presidential Decree” in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Grain Management Act (hereinafter referred to as the “Act”) means the following: <Amended on July 2, 2019>
1. Pulses, foxtail millet, hulled foxtail millet, sorghum, hulled sorghum, maize, buckwheat, oats, Job's tears, hulled Job's tears, proso millet, and hulled proso millet;
2. Hybrid grains of rice, barley and wheat, and the cereals specified in subparagraph 1;
3. Potatoes and sweet potatoes.
(2) “Products prescribed by Presidential Decree” in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act means the following:
1. Pressed products, crushed products, or agglomerated flour of rice, barley and wheat, and the cereals and tubers specified in paragraph (1);
2. Mixtures of the crushed products or flour specified in subparagraph 1 with other foods, without any change in their composition;
3. Dough made using only water from the crushed products or flour specified in subparagraph 1 or the mixtures under subparagraph 2;
4. Modified starches.
(3) “Grain prescribed by Presidential Decree” in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act means wheat and soybeans. <Added on September 17, 2013>

Article 2-2 (Grain Year)
The Government's grain year shall run from November 1 of the preceding year through October 31 of the relevant year.

Article 2-3 (Public Notice of Plans for Supply of and Demand for Government-Managed Grain)
Once a plan for supply of and demand for government-managed grain is finalized pursuant to Article 3 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs shall publicly notify its contents in the Official Gazette pursuant to paragraph (4) of that Article. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 3 (Scope of Producers, etc.)
(1) Producers under Article 4 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on December 22, 2015>
1. Farmers under subparagraph 2 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry;
2. Agricultural partnership corporations under Article 16 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities;
3. Agricultural corporations under Article 19 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities.
(2) Owners under Article 4 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on March 23, 2013; June 27, 2017>
1. Agricultural cooperatives, cooperative joint business corporations, and NongHyup Agribusiness Group under the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
2. Persons operating rice processing complexes under Article 22 (2) of the Act;
3. Other persons, such as grain dealers, whom the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs deems necessary for adjusting the supply of and demand for grain.

Article 4 Deleted. <June 30, 2005>

Article 5 (Advance Payments and Agreed Interest)
(1) The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may make an advance payment of up to 60 percent of the amount under a purchase agreement to a producer or owner who has entered into such an agreement pursuant to Article 4 (2) of the Act and wishes to receive an advance payment. <Amended on March 23, 2013>
(2) Where a producer or owner who has received an advance payment does not wish to perform the agreement, the agreed interest to be returned in addition to the advance payment pursuant to Article 4 (3) of the Act shall be the amount calculated by multiplying the advance payment corresponding to the quantity for which the producer or owner does not wish to perform the agreement, out of the agreed purchase quantity, by an annual interest rate of 5 percent. <Amended on September 17, 2013>

