Article 10 (Purposes for Which Government-Managed Grain May Be Sold)
“Purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 9 (1) 5 of the Act means the following: <Amended on September 19, 2017>
1. Relief;
2. Inventory clearance and emergency disposal;
3. Feed;
4. Import substitution;
5. Export;
6. Testing and research;
7. Development of processed products;
8. Overseas aid.

Article 11 (Sale of Government-Managed Grain on Credit)
(1) The purposes for which grain may be delivered before payment is received pursuant to the latter part of the part, other than the subparagraphs, of Article 9 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on September 17, 2013>
1. Use by State agencies and public use;
2. Relief (limited to cases where urgent delivery is necessary due to disasters or other such circumstances);
3. Inventory clearance and emergency disposal;
4. Import substitution;
5. General sale;
6. Processing and feed.
(2) The periods and conditions for sales on credit for the purposes under paragraph (1) shall be determined by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 12 (Public Notice of Selling Prices)
When the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs determines the selling price of government-managed grain pursuant to Article 9 (2) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly notify it without delay: Provided, That the selling price need not be publicly notified where purchasers of the relevant grain are limited to a small number of persons within a specified group. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 13 Deleted. <July 29, 1999>

Article 13-2 (Basis for Market Prices)
Market prices under Article 10 (3) of the Act shall be based on prices determined through public bidding or prices surveyed by the head of the National Data Office at the time of purchase or sale (where no prices have been surveyed by the head of the National Data Office, the wholesale market prices or actual transaction prices surveyed by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs). In such cases, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may, where necessary, present opinions to the head of the National Data Office concerning methods of price surveys and other relevant matters. <Amended on March 23, 2013; September 17, 2013; October 1, 2025>

Article 14 (Permission for Import)
(1) “Grain prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 12 (1) of the Act means the following:
1. Pressed products, crushed products, or agglomerated flour of rice;
2. Mixtures of crushed rice products or rice flour with other foods, without any change in their composition;
3. Dough made using only water from crushed rice products, rice flour, or the mixtures under subparagraph 2.
(2) A person who intends to import rice, etc. subject to permission pursuant to Article 12 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for permission to import rice, etc. (including an application in electronic form) to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 14-2 (Write-Offs)
“Cases recognized as having no prospect of collection as prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the death or disappearance of the delinquent payer” in Article 13-2 (4) 3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where the delinquent payer has died and collection is deemed unlikely;
2. Where the delinquent payer has been declared missing pursuant to Article 27 of the Civil Act and collection is deemed unlikely;
3. Where the whereabouts of the delinquent payer are unknown or the delinquent payer is found to have no property.

Article 15 Deleted. <July 29, 1999>

Article 16 (Purchase and Sale of Grain for Price Stabilization)
(1) “Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 16 (3) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on January 25, 2012; March 23, 2013; July 28, 2020>
1. The Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation under the Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the “Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation”);
2. Grain processors equipped with rice processing complex facilities;
3. Other persons designated by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs as being necessary for adjusting grain shipments and prices.
(2) “Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as where rice prices fluctuate sharply or are expected to fluctuate” in the proviso to Article 16 (4) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Added on July 28, 2020>
1. Where the quantity of rice produced in excess of the demand for rice in the relevant year reaches or exceeds the level prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs due to overproduction of rice or other such circumstances, causing or being expected to cause a sharp decline in rice prices;
2. Where rice prices fall or are expected to fall to or below the level prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs due to factors other than those under subparagraph 1.

Article 17 (Management of Rice Cultivation Area for Price Stabilization)
Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs intends to have the area under rice cultivation adjusted pursuant to Article 16-2 of the Act, the Minister shall consult with the Minister of Finance and Economy, the Minister of Planning and Budget, representatives of producers' organizations under subparagraph 4 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry, and other relevant persons regarding the cultivation area subject to adjustment, the methods of adjustment, and other matters necessary for adjusting cultivation areas. <Amended on December 30, 2025>

