Article 21 (Reporting of Grain Processing Businesses)
(1) "Grain processing businesses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 19 (1) of the Act means the following: <Amended 2010.3.15, 2013.3.23>
1. Flour milling business (meaning the business of manufacturing flour using grain, excluding tubers, as raw material);
2. Manufacturing business (meaning, among processing businesses using soybeans and corn as raw materials, manufacturing businesses of at least the scale prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs in consultation with the Minister of Health and Welfare);
3. Grain milling business of at least the scale prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs [meaning the business of producing polished rice, polished barley, hulled wheat, pressed barley, or split barley].
(2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 19 (1) of the Act means the following:
1. The name of the business operator (meaning the name of its representative in the case of a corporation);
2. The name of the business;
3. The location of the business;
4. The processing capacity of the business.
(3) "Grain processing businesses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19 (4) of the Act means the following: Provided, That manufacturing businesses falling under paragraph (1) 2 shall be excluded. <Amended 2020.7.28, 2021.2.17>
1. For persons who have obtained a manufacturing license under the Act on Liquor Licenses, etc.: Liquor manufacturing business;
2. For persons who have obtained a business license under the Food Sanitation Act: Seasoned food manufacturing business (limited to the manufacture of soybean paste, soy sauce, and red pepper paste), confectionery manufacturing business, tofu product manufacturing business, edible oil and fat manufacturing business, noodle manufacturing business, additive manufacturing business, sugar product manufacturing business, and food raw material processing business (limited to the manufacture of starches).

