Article 30-2 (Management of Debt Repayment)
Pursuant to Article 25-2 of the Act, the principal portion of debts shall be repaid in cash in a lump sum on the repayment due date: Provided, That where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs deems it necessary to repay all or part of the principal portion of debts before the repayment period expires, the Minister may make repayment in consultation with the Minister of Planning and Budget, specifically stating the following matters: <Amended 2013.3.23, 2025.12.30>
1. The scheduled repayment date;
2. Details of the debts to be repaid;
3. The principal to be repaid and interest thereon;
4. Other matters necessary for repayment.

Article 30-3 (Establishment of an Account for the Grain Bonds Liquidation Fund)
The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs shall establish a fund account at the Bank of Korea to clearly account for the revenue and expenditure of the Grain Bonds Liquidation Fund under Article 25 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Fund"). <Amended 2013.3.23>

Article 30-4 (Uses of the Fund)
"Those prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25-3 (2) 2 of the Act means interest on borrowings.

Article 31 (Projects Eligible for Loans and Subsidies)
(1) The scope of projects for which necessary funds may be loaned or subsidies may be paid within the budget pursuant to Article 26 of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Projects that incur losses due to increases in the price of raw grain among projects for processing and selling grain to improve the people's dietary habits and stabilize grain supply and demand;
2. Projects entrusted by the Government to nonprofit corporations to improve the people's dietary habits;
3. Projects concerning the establishment and operation of grain markets;
4. Survey and research projects concerning improvements in grain distribution;
5. Projects concerning improvements in grain management methods and facilities;
6. Projects concerning improvements in facilities and equipment for storing government-managed grain or preparing grain.
(2) Prior consultation with the Minister of Planning and Budget shall be conducted regarding the terms of loans under paragraph (1), such as interest on the loans. <Amended 2025.12.30>

Article 32 (Supervision)
Pursuant to Article 27 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may order grain owners, grain dealers, grain processing business operators, and persons who export, import, store, or transport grain to submit reports according to the following categories, specifying the institution to receive the reports, the reporting deadline, and the scope of persons subject to reporting: <Amended 2013.3.23, 2019.7.2>
1. Grain owners: The quantity of grain owned;
2. Grain dealers: Grain purchase and sale prices and inventory quantities by type of grain;
3. Grain processing business operators: Purchases of raw grain and quantities of products produced, packaged, sold, and held in inventory;
4. Grain exporters and importers: Export and import quantities and prices by exporting or importing country, and the uses of imported grain;
5. Grain storage business operators: The quality condition of grain in storage, inventory quantities, quantities received into storage, quantities released from storage, and quantities affected by accidents;
6. Grain transport business operators: Quantities of grain transported by point of departure and destination, names of cargo owners, quantities in storage, quantities affected by accidents, means of transport, and transport capacity.

Article 32-2 (Payment of Monetary Rewards)
(1) Monetary rewards under Article 27-3 of the Act shall be paid, within a limit of 1 million won, to persons who report or file an accusation concerning a violation falling under any of the subparagraphs of that Article with a relevant administrative agency or investigative agency.
(2) The criteria, methods, procedures, etc. for payment of monetary rewards under paragraph (1) shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. <Amended 2013.3.23>

Article 33 Deleted <1997.12.31>

Article 34 (Delegation and Entrustment of Authority)
(1) Pursuant to Article 29 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs shall delegate the following authority to the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Do Governors, or Special Self-Governing Province Governors: <Amended 2013.3.23, 2015.6.30>
1. Sale of government-managed grain for use by State agencies or for public use under Article 9 (1) of the Act;
1-2. Sale of government-managed grain for processing under Article 9 (1) of the Act [excluding affairs concerning the allocation of quantities to be supplied for sale to rice processors under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on Promotion of the Rice Processing Industry and Rice Utilization (hereinafter referred to as "rice processors")];
2. Supervision of grain owners, grain dealers, grain processing business operators, and persons who export, import, store, or transport grain under the subparagraphs of Article 27 (1) of the Act, and issuance of identification certificates to investigating public officials (excluding supervision and issuance of identification certificates to investigating public officials under paragraph (2) 1);
3. Imposition and collection of administrative fines on persons falling under Article 36 (1) 5 of the Act.
(2) Pursuant to Article 29 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs shall delegate the following authority to the Director General of the National Agricultural Products Quality Management Service: <Amended 2013.3.23, 2015.6.30>
1. Supervision of grain owners, grain dealers, and grain processing business operators falling under Article 27 (1) 1 through 3 of the Act (limited to investigations into use or disposition for purposes other than the designated uses under Article 9 (4) of the Act, investigations into labeling and advertising under Articles 20-2 and 20-3 of the Act, and investigations into the distribution or sale of mixed grain under Article 20-4 (2) of the Act), and issuance of identification certificates to investigating public officials;
2. Commissioning and operation of honorary monitors under Article 27-2 of the Act;
3. Payment of monetary rewards under Article 27-3 of the Act;
4. Imposition and collection of administrative fines on persons falling under Article 36 (1) 6 of the Act.
(3) Where the Director General of the National Agricultural Products Quality Management Service redelegates part of the authority delegated pursuant to paragraph (2) to the heads of subordinate agencies pursuant to the latter part of Article 6 (1) of the Government Organization Act, the Director General shall publicly notify the details thereof.
(4) Pursuant to Article 29 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may entrust the following affairs to the Korea Agro-Fisheries and Food Trade Corporation, an agriculture-related institution, or an agriculture-related organization: <Amended 2012.1.25, 2013.3.23, 2015.6.30>
1. Sale of government-managed grain for processing under Article 9 (1) of the Act (limited to affairs concerning the allocation of quantities to be supplied for sale to rice processors);
2. Stockpiling and operation of grain under the Agreement on the ASEAN Plus Three Emergency Rice Reserve among grain held in public reserve under Article 10 (1) of the Act (including affairs concerning purchase, storage, transport, sale, and aid);
3. Import of grain (limited to rice) under Article 11 of the Act (including affairs concerning transport and storage associated with imports);
4. Sale under Article 9 (1) of the Act of grain imported pursuant to Article 11 of the Act (limited to rice) (excluding sale for use by State agencies, for processing, or for public use).
(5) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs entrusts duties pursuant to paragraph (4), the Minister shall publicly notify the entrusted person, the entrusted duties, etc. <Added 2015.6.30>

Article 34-2 (Processing of Unique Identifying Information)
(1) The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs (including persons performing the duties of the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs on the Minister's behalf pursuant to Article 24 of the Act and persons to whom the authority of the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs has been delegated, entrusted, or redelegated pursuant to Article 34 of this Decree) may process materials containing resident registration numbers under subparagraph 1 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act where it is unavoidable for the performance of the following affairs: <Amended 2020.7.28>
1. Affairs concerning the purchase of grain under Article 4 of the Act;
2. Affairs concerning the sale of government-managed grain under Article 9 of the Act;
3. Affairs concerning restrictions on eligibility to purchase government-managed grain under Article 9-2 of the Act;
4. Affairs concerning the purchase and sale of grain held in public reserve under Article 10 of the Act;
5. Affairs concerning the purchase and sale of grain under Article 16 of the Act;
6. Affairs concerning loans or payment of subsidies under Articles 22 (2) and 26 of the Act;
7. Affairs concerning supervision under Article 27 of the Act;
8. Affairs concerning payment of monetary rewards under Article 27-3 of the Act.
(2) The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs (including persons to whom the authority of the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs has been delegated or redelegated pursuant to Article 34), the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, Do Governors, Special Self-Governing Province Governors, or heads of Sis/Guns/Gus (including persons to whom the relevant authority has been delegated or entrusted, where such authority has been delegated or entrusted) may process materials containing resident registration numbers under subparagraph 1 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act where it is unavoidable for the performance of affairs concerning the operation of honorary monitors under Article 27-2 of the Act.

